@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix : <http://example.org/ontology#>.

### Classes ###
:Person a owl:Class.
:Project a owl:Class.
:Skill a owl:Class.
:Ontology a owl:Class.
:Domain a owl:Class.
:Vehicle a owl:Class.
:Car a owl:Class.
:Truck a owl:Class.
:Motorcycle a owl:Class.
:DomainExpert a owl:Class.
:Work a owl:Class.
:Process a owl:Class.
:Issue a owl:Class.
:Solution a owl:Class.
:System a owl:Class.
:Application a owl:Class.

### Object Properties ###
:hasRole a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Person;
    rdfs:range :Project.

:hasSkill a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Person;
    rdfs:range :Skill.

:hasSkillLevel a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Person;
    rdfs:range :Skill.

:requiresSkill a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Project;
    rdfs:range :Skill.

:Accuracy a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Ontology;
    rdfs:range :Domain.

:Intended a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Domain;
    rdfs:range :Ontology.

:Representation a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Domain;
    rdfs:range :Ontology.

:hasType a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Vehicle;
    rdfs:range owl:Thing.

:hasColor a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Vehicle;
    rdfs:range xsd:string.

:hasEngineSize a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Vehicle;
    rdfs:range xsd:string.

:hasMaxSpeed a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:domain :Vehicle;
    rdfs:range xsd:string.

...

### Individuals ###
:John a :Person;
    :hasRole :ProjectA;
    :hasSkill :Programming;
    :hasSkillLevel :Expert.

:ProjectA a :Project;
    :requiresSkill :Programming.

:Car a :Vehicle.

...

### Comments ###
# Assuming that the property "hasType" for Vehicle can have multiple ranges like Car, Truck, Motorcycle.

# Add more comments as needed for clarity.

This is a simplified example of how the ontology could be structured based on the provided triples and individuals. The actual ontology structure may vary based on additional information or requirements.